00:55:00,000 --> 00:55:06,000
True Grit is a 2010 American Western film produced, written,
and directed by Joel Coen and Ethan Coen.

14
00:59:13,846 --> 00:59:19,846
It is an adaptation of Charles Portis's 1968 novel.

15
01:03:27,692 --> 01:03:33,692
Starring Jeff Bridges and Hailee Steinfeld (in her theatrical film debut),
True Grit also stars Matt Damon, Josh Brolin, and Barry Pepper.

16
01:07:41,538 --> 01:07:47,538
In the film, 14-year-old farm girl Mattie Ross (Steinfeld) hires boozy, trigger-happy lawman Rooster Cogburn (Bridges) to go after outlaw Tom Chaney
(Brolin), who murdered her father, accompanied by Texas Ranger LaBoeuf (Damon), who is also hunting Chaney, and who has his own gripes with Cogburn.

17
01:11:55,384 --> 01:12:01,384
The Coens intended their film to be a more faithful adaptation of Portis's novel than the 1969 version
starring John Wayne; in particular, they wanted to tell the story from Mattie's point of view.

18
01:16:09,230 --> 01:16:15,230
The casting call for the role of Mattie received some 15,000
applicants before Steinfeld was selected.

19
01:20:23,076 --> 01:20:29,076
Principal photography occurred mainly in the Santa Fe,
New Mexico, area in March–April 2010.

20
01:24:36,923 --> 01:24:42,923
True Grit was shot by cinematographer Roger Deakins and scored by composer Carter Burwell—both Coen
regulars—while the brothers themselves edited the film, under the Roderick Jaynes pseudonym.

21
01:28:50,769 --> 01:28:56,769
True Grit was released in theatres in the United States by
Paramount Pictures on December 22, 2010.

22
01:33:04,615 --> 01:33:10,615
The film grossed $252 million worldwide on a $35–38 million production budget, and was very well received by critics, with particular praise
for its acting, directing, writing, score, and production values, with some deeming it superior to the earlier adaptation.

23
01:37:18,461 --> 01:37:24,461
Rated one of the best films of 2010, True Grit received several awards and nominations; at the 83rd
Academy Awards, it received 10 nominations, including Best Picture, but won none.

24
01:41:32,307 --> 01:41:38,307
The film explores themes of bounty hunter, based on novel or book,
father murder, loss of loved one, texas ranger.

25
01:45:46,153 --> 01:45:52,153
The tone is emotional.
